;; state.corpus -- mutable-reference-type gap corpus (pending). Every
;; form on this list currently DIVERGES between real Clojure 1.13.0-
;; alpha6 and mova; it is a ledger of failures, not aspirational syntax.
;; One session -- a `def` on an earlier line is visible to later lines.
;;
;; Headline finding: mova has ONLY a bare, unary-constructor `atom` +
;; `deref`/`swap!`/`reset!` + `future`/`future?`. Everything else in
;; Clojure's reference-type family is completely absent (unresolved
;; symbol): atom construction options (`:validator`/`:meta`),
;; `add-watch`/`remove-watch`, `compare-and-set!`, `swap-vals!`/
;; `reset-vals!`, the ENTIRE volatile family (`volatile!`/`vswap!`/
;; `vreset!`/`volatile?`), the ENTIRE ref/STM family (`ref`/`dosync`/
;; `alter`/`commute`/`ref-set`), the ENTIRE agent family (`agent`/
;; `send`/`await`), `future-cancel`/`future-done?`/`future-cancelled?`,
;; `pmap`, `locking`, and `with-open`. `swap!`/`reset!`/plain `deref` on
;; a plain atom already conform (excluded here, not repeated).
;;
;; Cascading-state note: several `@x` reads below stay at their PREVIOUS
;; value in mova (e.g. `@cs` never advances past 1) not because the read
;; itself is broken, but because the upstream mutator on the prior line
;; (`compare-and-set!`, `add-watch`'s watch-fn, ...) already failed as an
;; unresolved symbol and never ran -- kept because the downstream VALUE
;; divergence is real and worth pinning independently of the upstream
;; cause.
;;
;; `deref` with an explicit timeout was probed and found to conform
;; trivially (atoms/already-completed futures are always immediately
;; ready) -- an actually-elapsed-timeout scenario would need a real delay
;; primitive mova doesn't have (no `Thread/sleep` interop), and any
;; wall-clock-based construction would violate this corpus family's
;; determinism rule, so that specific dimension is left untested here.
(some? (atom 1 :validator pos?))
(:doc (meta (atom 1 :meta {:doc "x"})))
(def wlog (atom []))
(def wa (atom 0))
(do (add-watch wa :k (fn [k r o n] (swap! wlog conj [o n]))) :watched)
(do (swap! wa inc) @wlog)
(do (remove-watch wa :k) :unwatched)
(do (swap! wa inc) @wlog)
(def cs (atom 1))
(compare-and-set! cs 1 2)
@cs
(compare-and-set! cs 1 99)
@cs
(def svs (atom 1))
(def v (volatile! 1))
(def ag (agent 0))
(do (send ag inc) :sent)
(await ag)
@ag
(def f1 (future (+ 1 2)))
(do @f1 (future-done? f1))
(future-cancel f1)
(future-cancelled? f1)
(def lockobj (atom :m))
(with-open [x (java.io.StringWriter.)] (.write x "hi") (str x))
